---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/base';
---
<Guide
  title="Getting your web address"
  heading="Getting your"
  thin="web address."
  intro="Your web address — your domain — is what people type to find you. You buy it yourself so it is registered in your name and you own it outright. About fifteen minutes, and around eleven dollars for the first year."
  description="How to buy your own domain name at Porkbun and connect it to your Weaver Digital website."
>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Why you buy it and not me.</strong> It is registered in your name, so it stays yours whatever happens. I never hold your domain name.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>The walkthrough</h2>
    <p>The whole thing is in one short guide — every screen you will see, with a picture of each one and the exact thing to click. Open it on your phone and work through it on your computer, or print it.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-blue" href={url('/guides/getting-your-domain-name.pdf')} download>
        Download the walkthrough <span class="arrow">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p>Have three things ready before you sit down: your business email, a card for the first year, and two or three name ideas. Not sure about the names? Send them to me first and I will check them.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>Two things to be careful about</h2>
    <p>Everything else in the guide can be changed later. These two cannot.</p>
    <div class="note warn">
      <p><strong>Check the spelling before you pay.</strong> Porkbun gives no refunds, and a domain name cannot be changed afterwards. Read it twice on the checkout screen.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="note warn">
      <p><strong>Tell me first if you already use email on that address</strong> — something like you@yourbusiness.com. Your email runs off the same settings as your website, and I would rather be careful than take your email down for an afternoon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>When you are done, tell me</h2>
    <p>Email or text me the address you bought. I finish the connection at my end and let you know the moment your website is live — usually within a day.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:ashley@weaverdigital.io?subject=My%20domain%20name">Email ashley@weaverdigital.io <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>Already have a domain name?</h2>
    <p>Then skip all of this. Tell me your web address and I will take it from there — <a href={url('/guides/domain-you-already-own')}>a domain you already own</a> covers the few ways to give me what I need, wherever the name is registered.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>If I need to get in there later</h2>
    <p>Every so often something has to change in your Porkbun account — email on your own address, say, or a setting that stopped working. You can add me as an <a href={url('/guides/porkbun-authorized-user')}>authorized user</a> so I can do it without ever knowing your password. It is free, and you can remove me whenever you like. Nothing to do about it now.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>Once your address is pointed at your site, I will send you a link to sign in so you can see it and make changes yourself. That is the <a href={url('/guides/signing-in')}>next guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Guide>
